# Request review from @eblume on every PR, so an agent-opened one lands in the
# "Review requests" filter instead of no queue at all. A review request is a
# notification, not a gate: nothing here blocks a merge.
#
# Patterns are Go regexps anchored as `^…$` against each changed path, not
# gitignore globs. GitHub's `*` catch-all does not compile and Forgejo skips the
# rule silently, leaving a file that looks right and does nothing; `.*` is the
# equivalent that works.
#
# Forgejo reads this from the default branch of the base repo when a PR opens,
# and only then. It skips drafts and WIP PRs, and never requests review from the
# PR's own author.
.*  @eblume
